propositions.answer:
Crowd Crush can occur in the following situations:
- When a moving crowd is funneled into a smaller and smaller space;
- When a crowd meets an obstacle (such as a dead end, or a locked door);
- or when an already densely-packed crowd has an influx of people, causing a pressure wave towards those at the front of the crowd.
- The people entering the crowd may be unaware of the effect on those in front and continue to press in.

When crowds are not too tightly packed, you still have time to make the decision to leave for your own safety. Be aware of when a crowd crush situation may be developing, and leave early while escape is still an option.
